@fm description | description | How the two tills at Crumbwick Bakery are opened, used and counted.
# Tills
s description | There are two tills, one at the street door and one at the pickup shelf.
s description | Each till has its own drawer key, and the keys live in the sconce room.
## Opening a till
s gate{till_float} | Count the float in the drawer before you log in.
s rule | Log in with your own crew number.
s prohibition{till_share} | Never share a crew number with another person.
s example | For example, a shared number made it impossible to find who had given a wrong change on a Saturday.
s description | The float is eighty pounds in coins and notes.
## Taking payment
l gate | Say the total aloud before the customer pays
l rule{till_receipt} | Offer a receipt with every sale
l prohibition | Do not open the drawer without a sale
l prohibition{till_card} | Do not write a card number on paper
l description | The card reader sits on the left of each till
## Mistakes
s rule{till_void} | Call the shop manager to void a sale, and wait for the manager to key the void.
s gate | Keep the receipt of the wrong sale before the manager voids it.
s prohibition{till_ownvoid} | Never void your own sale.
s example | Case: a crew member voided a sale of two loaves and kept the cash, and the count was short by that amount.
s description | The shop manager holds the void key on a red cord.
## Counting
s rule | Count the drawer twice at closing and write both counts in the book.
s gate | Ask a second person to count it if the two counts differ.
s description | A difference of more than two pounds is reported to the shop manager.
s rule | Take your time with the count.
